LDAP

A Plug-In for Mill. Put it in the "Mill Plug-Ins" folder.

  ldap://host/                              The server's directories
  ldap://host/dn                            An entry
  ldap://host/dn?attributes?scope?filter    A search

The scope is base, one, or sub; the filter is as RFC 1960 has it, such as
(cn=Smith*). Lightweight Directory Access Protocol, version 2 (version 3 for
a server that takes only that). Read-only. Results as records (each entry
a small table) or one table, from Settings or the address (x-layout=table).
Values that aren't text are shown by their size. When the server asks,
Mill asks for a DN and password.

plugin://ldap/about has a form, filled in from Settings.

Written from the published specifications (RFC 1777, 1779, 1959,
1960, 2251, 2254, 2255, and X.690's Basic Encoding Rules).

Build: ./build.sh writes build/LDAP.bin.
